/* Shown when a configured endpoint answered and can be used. */
"Ready" = "Ready";

/* ── fixtures for the localisation tests ──────────────────────────
   Not shown anywhere. They exist because two facts about the mechanism can
   only be established by running it, and both are silent when wrong:

    • which key a Swift interpolation actually produces — `%@` for a String
      but `%lld` for an Int. `scripts/check.sh` reads the keys the compiler
      emits rather than deriving them, and this is the fact that made reading
      the source untenable: telling those two apart needs the type checker;
    • that a key nobody translated comes back as itself.

   The values are markers rather than sentences so a passing test cannot be
   confused with a working screen. */
"%lld things" = "MARKER-LLD %lld";
"%@ things" = "MARKER-AT %@";
